{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Karush-Kuhn-Tucker Conditions.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Karush-Kuhn-Tucker Conditions.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"karush kuhn tucker conditions karush kuhn tucker conditions","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Karush-Kuhn-Tucker Conditions.md","fileName":"Karush-Kuhn-Tucker Conditions.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Karush-Kuhn-Tucker Conditions","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 19:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Nonlinear Optimization Methods]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Nonlinear Optimization Methods","Lagrange Multiplier Method","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Karush-Kuhn-Tucker Conditions.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Karush-Kuhn-Tucker Conditions.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"karush kuhn tucker conditions karush kuhn tucker conditions","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Karush-Kuhn-Tucker Conditions.md","fileName":"Karush-Kuhn-Tucker Conditions.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Karush-Kuhn-Tucker Conditions","heading":"Karush-Kuhn-Tucker Conditions","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The Karush-Kuhn-Tucker conditions extend [[Lagrange Multiplier Method|Lagrange multiplier reasoning]] to inequality constraints. They combine primal feasibility, multiplier sign restrictions, stationarity, and complementary slackness.\n\nComplementary slackness connects each multiplier to its constraint: an inactive inequality has zero multiplier, while a positive multiplier can occur only for an active constraint. Under convexity conditions, the conditions can also be sufficient for optimality.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Nonlinear Optimization Methods","Lagrange Multiplier Method","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf"],"pr